{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\uc1 \deff0\deflang1033\deflangfe1033{\fonttbl{\f0\froman\fcharset0\fprq2{\*\panose 02020603050405020304}Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;}{\stylesheet{\nowidctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang3081 \snext0 Normal;}{\*\cs10 \additive Default Paragraph Font;}}{\*\listtable{\list\listtemplateid-1\listsimple{\listlevel\levelnfc0\leveljc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat0\levelspace0\levelindent0{\leveltext\'01*;}{\levelnumbers;}}{\listname ;}\listid-2}}{\*\listoverridetable{\listoverride\listid-2\listoverridecount1{\lfolevel\listoverrideformat{\listlevel\levelnfc23\leveljc0\levelfollow0\levelstartat0\levelold\levelspace0\levelindent360{\leveltext\'01-;}{\levelnumbers;}\fi-360\li360 }}\ls1}}{\info{\title 497 }{\author corporate licence user}{\operator Ben Groenen}{\creatim\yr1998\mo8\dy26\hr22\min9}{\revtim\yr1998\mo8\dy26\hr22\min9}{\printim\yr1998\mo5\dy11\hr18\min49}{\version2}{\edmins1}{\nofpages5}{\nofwords3345}{\nofchars19070}{\*\company Groenen}{\nofcharsws23419}{\vern71}}\paperw11907\paperh16840\margl1797\margr1797 \widowctrl\ftnbj\aenddoc\hyphcaps0\formshade\viewkind1\viewscale117\viewzk2 \fet0\sectd \psz9\linex0\headery709\footery709\colsx709\endnhere\sectdefaultcl {\*\pnseclvl1\pnucrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta .}}{\*\pnseclvl2\pnucltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta .}}{\*\pnseclvl3\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta .}}{\*\pnseclvl4\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl5\pndec\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl6\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl7\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl8\pnlcltr\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}{\*\pnseclvl9\pnlcrm\pnstart1\pnindent720\pnhang{\pntxtb (}{\pntxta )}}\pard\plain \nowidctlpar\adjustright \fs20\lang3081 {497 \tab - 10 knights & Gilbert
\par 499 \tab - 18 knights (including Hwyll, Edar, Tathyl & Nai) & Gilbert
\par \tab - Autumn - Arcavius Marries Margot
\par 500\tab - Jeanne gives birth to twins (Gwen & Gwyn), Morgaine is 14 (time to be married), Arthur is 8, Caradoc is 4, Nia is 1
\par 
\par - word has reached me that Anglia has been taken by more Saxons - Earl Robert has chosen me to investigate with some of the other Lords\rquote  men to find out if these Saxons are going to link up with the other Saxons - Arcavius for Praetor meets me & Hwyll in Sarum, & we go to Levcomagus & with Cynan to Silchester to Staines to London - learn of sword in stone \ldblquote  whomsoever pulleth out the sword is the rightful king of England\rdblquote  - has been there for 5 years - test it - get Arcavius to confirm what it says - to Hertford to Royston - visit sister - go to Cambridge - it has a number of Iceni who have fled from Anglia - Cynan advises getting a guide - I orate (fail) & Cilydd steps forward & will take us if we do justice on those Saxons that burnt his village - I agree
\par - our plan = go to village & eliminate opposition - kill em, but take a chief or leader-type prisoner to get information needed - on trip there, try & avoid fighting
\par - leave at dawn - E a couple of days - nearing Cilydd\rquote s village - the village has been burnt down - order Hwyll to look for tracks & Arcavius to look for anything
\par - Madog (Hwyll\rquote s new squire) has found something - Hwyll goes over to hime & he\rquote s chortling, trying not to laugh - I look around & find a dead body to the side - it has its arm & side eaten away - go to speak with Hwyll - Madog says he found a dragon\rquote s tracks, but Hwyll is pointing out its a combination of 4 tracks - I bring Hwyll to weird corpse - we discuss its like the goblin\rquote s blood, but the arm being eaten away meant it was a giant - a Fomori - I (critically) find tracks - we go tracking, late in afternoon, Hwyll leading his horse - backtracks & thinks trail went one way while Cynan thinks trail went the other way - party splits up, plan = for 1/2 hour & then we come back to that point - Hwyll & me with squires & Cilydd go 1 way, the others the other - 10 minutes after splitting, a big roar & a 4-armed, armored giant swings giant club & knocks Hwyll over - I inspired to save my good & noble friend & vassal, charge & fight Fomori - hit him critically once, knocking him down, as he\rquote s getting up & squatting he grapples my horse, I swing & critical him again - I make horse roll & leap off horse - my sword has been eaten away & is still being eaten away - 3 Saxons are fighting Hwyll & the 2 squires & 3 Saxons are facing me - I throw stub of sword at Saxons & fight defensively with shield - Cynan & Arcavius come charging ahorseback - they fight Saxons who are facing me - the 2 knights take out the Saxons - the others had only 1 Saxon (who was berserking) & they were letting him rave himself out, but Cynan steps in & takes him out
\par - camp at Saxon\rquote s camp - on Arcavius\rquote  watch, he yells at something in forest, we wake & Cilydd calls out to forest
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Pedrog \endash  stay = escaped from an encampment \endash  lost in forest for days \endash  he was originally taken before winter! \endash  3 other prisoners \endash  he escaped when the Saxons were distracted by 2 powerful Saxons came a visiting \endash  us knights chat, Cilydd climb tree in morning & we go in morning \endash  Cilydd & Budd climbed tree, haze was to S (some place on fire), there was smaller fires (camps) to N nearer Fens \endash  speaking with Pedrog & asking him whether he remembered Fens, he said he remembered the smell
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {We head N \endash  as we travel, notice that we cross Pedrog\rquote s wandering trail N- As we travel, Arc sees a shine of metal ahead, we tried to wait but I couldn\rquote t see enough cover to ambush them \endash  so we rode straight at them, there are 6 Saxons (2 of which are big uns) \endash  me & Cyn go at them \endash  Cyn down in first blow, I knock mine down (it\rquote s a chieftain) \endash  I inspired to protect Cyn, as Chief getting up, I strike at 1 of 2 fighting Hwy \endash  then next round I fight Chief, 2 more blows and he goes down \endash  Hwy & squire against 1 now, berserker who took Cyn down and 1 other are fighting Arc \endash  I attack berserker \endash  1 blow normal, 2}{\super nd}{ blow cleft him in half \endash  battle finishes \endash  Arc & then Hwy 1}{\super st}{ aid Cyn, I 1}{\super st}{ aid Saxon chief \endash  we head back to Cambridge & will head back to Royston
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Traveling SE to Cambridge \endash  hear sounds ahead \endash  I take Hwy ahead & meet with 2 coming from SE to NE, also heading to Cambridge \endash  they are Iceni \endash  women \ldblquote warriors\rdblquote  \endash  we talk \endash  they are led by Colomb Not-A-Lady \endash  I notice we\rquote re being outflanked 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {We agree to join our forces \endash  I spout how well we\rquote ve done \endash  one of the Iceni chirurges Cyn, butthey all dislike the Saxon & Arc (Roman)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Getting to Cambridge, find out the Iceni are going to Warwick as they have kin there \endash  we (party) are talking about overcrowding \endash  travelling to Royston taking 100s of Iceni \endash  Arc suggests we could visit the Lady who is known for rescueing Cymric people
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {I decide all party including Saxon & … Colomb \endash  I persuade her to come & find out about this \ldblquote place of safety\rdblquote  - we ride out tof Cambridge & once out of sight gather all horses & people in a clump & when Arc does his stuff & we all seem to fly alone & then we appear by tree which Arc fll out of - we travel to cutting & in ther tell Arc to go ahead & warn of our coming - we ... ?
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {...
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {speaking in feast hall - we decide we need to gather all Iceni refugees to Cambridge, for forwarding to here, & also we need to capture a Fomori
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {we all, except Cyn & Owain, go to hall next morn & ask to speak to the Lady - the horses are ready & await outside - the Lady is giving folk-dancing lessons to the young ones - when there\rquote s an easing in the dancing (it just doesn\rquote t stop), we inform the Lady that its time for us to leave & create the cairn & we request her aid in allowing Cyn to remain in her gracious care - she asks whos going back (to where & when) & I say just us - so she sends us back ... without the horses. In the blink of an eye, we\rquote re on a road track, I set the squires to gathering rocks - an old couple & their livestock are travelling S on the track & stop & gawk - Arc asks where the road leads to & finds out we\rquote re 1 1/2 miles N of Cambridge
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Head S (walking in armour) - after a mile, there\rquote s a noticeable tree (large, gnarly, hangs over track & has Latin grafitti etched into it), after looking around get squires to build a cairn behind the tree
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Arc places the refugee stone amidst the pile - we then walk to Cambridge, in spite of Colomb\rquote s urgings to go back & get the horses - when we get to Cambridge, she goes to gather her supporters & the rest of us rest - she comes back & informs us that she has spoken to her group & has convinced another group of the same size - we head back to the cairn & she says show us how to go - I step forward to the cairn, & after a while think of going to the place of safety - I find myself at the bottom of stairs leading up to gateway, with gargoyles lined up - speak to gardener & then direct some of the Cymrics up the stairs - ....
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {bath & then dinner - ...
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {next morn, we are transported back to 10 minutes after we left, say goodbye to Colomb & head E - that night we camp & during my watch, a faun visits Annwyn - in morn, Annwyn says we need to go S & I find out what the faun told him - 5 miles S, Annwyn gets off his horse, strings bow & tells us to be quiet, Arc off horse & Cyn off horse - Annwyn goes forward shoots twice followed by two cries - Fomori comes charging out & Cyn faces him, the rest of us face up to the 4 Saxons - me onto 2 of them - 1st round I major one of them & knock him down & Cyn major wounds the giant - next round, nothing much happens except Arc is knocked down - then I majorly, majorly kill one, Hwyll kills his & Arc knocked down again - then Hwyll kills the one standing over Arc, I kill my remaining one & Cyn brings down the Fomori - Arc 1st aids the giant back to +ves & then the Saxon - Annwyn goes to get the Lady - Hwyll 1st aids Arc - the Saxons are separated from their goods
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {The Lady & Annwyn arrive, we move the giant so it\rquote s resting on its back against a tree - she talks to him - gets Cyn to threaten him but it doesn\rquote t work - she growls (like a dragon) at the giant & the giant blabs - the Fomori King has offered the Angle King a great treasure for 2 brides for the Fomori
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}bye-bye prisoners
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}we talk around what we want to do - eventually, after talking about demons (not Gorboduc), I suggest we go ask the fish
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}vision shown by fish is of a church, small with an angel hand on sword hilt & other holding a spear - Arc asks how do we stop the Saxon/Fomori alliance - Annwyn says he doesn\rquote t think the Wise One will answer just as the Salmon shows a very beautiful queen (?) / Saxon - Arc & I remember about rumours of the Jutish-Saxon king\rquote s wife being extremely beautiful
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}as we are ready to depart, Hwyll throws an acorn & asks to see Morgawse - see a twisted, bitter woman who turns around & sees us & scares the fish - she must have been taught by the Witch of the N (as mentioned in 496)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}we travelled back to the castle & discussed our plans some more \endash  our decision is to send Arcavius to Bishop Baldwin to get him to strengthen the protection at Glastonbury while Cynan & I go to Silchester to tell Duke Ulfius of the new Saxon situation (they are not allied/connected to the currently resident Saxons, but they are allie to the Fomori) and to convince him to make common cause with Earl Robert and Praetor Jonathel of Dorset \endash  From there, we would journey to Salisbury to do the same with Earl Robert.  Each of us offers to provide our service for the Lady when she requires it of us.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Arcavius and Gessius are sent a week prior to the fight with the Fomori, and ½ mile from the Bishop\rquote s residence … [I DIDN\rquote T WRITE UP WHAT HAPPENED TO HIM]
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}The day after the fight with the Fomori, we reappear in the Amphitheatre which was just off to the north of Silchester.  We go straight to Duke Ulfius\rquote  court. Politicking allows me to pick out all the factions of this court.  Just like Salisbury, really.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}After arranging a private meeting, we tell our story as: \ldblquote We are returning from the important scouting mission about the latest Saxon meeting.  Cynan, the Steward of Levcomagus, reports tp his vassal lord.  The new Saxons are not allied to the established Saxon tribes.  However, they are allied to the Fomori giants, like the one that we killed in the caverns below the city.  As proof, we show some of the Fomori equipment we retrieved.  Cynan also talks of the great treasure offered by the Saxons to the Fomori, which is being held at Glastonbury Tor.  Sir Arcavius had been sent to request reinforcements for the Tor from Bishop Baldwin.  Cynan passes on my suggestion of a more formal alliance between Silchester and Salisbury.  I expand on it to include as many Cymric and Roman lords as we can for the defence of all.  I suggest the reforming of the Council of Lords/Regents (whatever it was before) which would provide leadership for such an alliance.  The conversation wavers over to the High Kingship and the sword in the stone and a resulting possible ruler & I throw the comment that maybe that would provide someone with no affiliation to just one land & as a result the strong-willed lords would be more willing to follow such a one.  But returning to the point, Ulfius raises the question of how to break such an alliance \endash  Feeling compelled to find some answer to the puzzling vision shown to us by the Wise One (very fishy), I tell of how we were shown a vision of a very beautiful Saxon princess/queen, whereon Cynan mentions we thought it might be the Jute queen.  Ulfius questions how we got this vision, & I gave him the truth which he wouldn\rquote t have believed if we hadn\rquote t shown him the Fomori were involved/  In discussing what to do, I suggested that we conduct raids on the Saxons in Essex … killing all we fought and leaving behind broken bits of the Fomori stuff we had found so that we might cause dissension between the new and the old Saxons.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Ulfius & Cynan suggested we concentrate on the Jutes in this, but any raids on the Kent-Silchester border would pass suspicion onto us & we wouldn\rquote t survive long by boat on the coast where we wouldn\rquote t be able to penetrate/infiltrate that far.  I told Ulfius that for too long the Saxons had profited from our divisiveness & now was the time to repay what we had learnt
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Other places that we would like to sound out for this alliance were
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li720\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Londinium, which was ruled by a council & had about 70 knights & 1000 soldiers
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li720\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Malahaut, a kingdom ruled by the King of 100 knights (who had about 300 knights & 2000 soldiers
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li720\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Idris, the King of Cornwall, and maybe Mark of Totnes
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li720\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Duke Cornius of Lindsey, who commanded about 300 knights and 1000 soldiers
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {We stay overnight, then travel 1 day to Levcomagus, then travel 1 day to Sarum where we bring Earl Robert into the fold [I DIDN\rquote T WRITE THE CONVERSATION UP] \endash  Then we travel on to Vogon castle
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {We choose to travel so we camp away from the castle.  On my watch, Puck appears with an invitation (?) for me to see Oberon. I wake up the others & Cynan suggests he doesn\rquote t want to go & I review that the Fae can delay our return & I think he probably wants us to go get the Cauldron now, but our mission is urgent.  So only Budd and I go with Puck.  We are supposed to meet up with the others at Glastonbury Tor.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Speak with Oberon and I piss him off mightily (I say no … and maybe one or two other things).  One of the offers I recall is the use of the sword Marius for the duration of my life (can\rquote t remember now why I refused … was it a choice of loyalty between Arthur and Oberon? not sure)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {We go head south to Dorset \endash  I stop off home while the rest continue south.  Speak to Jeanne about what has happened during this season, and especially about pissing off Oberon.  She is sorry but she cannot help with some of my enemies.  I pass on the invitation from the Lady.  Jeanne brings up the topic of Morgaine.  She had seemed moody when I had returned, but I had thought it was something of her age (teens?!), but she has apparently had a lover (!) which no-one had seen.  This raised thought that she was of an age for matching.  I tried to think of possible matches ( I don\rquote t know .. the name Gondarins seems to spring to mind)  and hoped she would be as likely as I had been with my match.  [YES, I KNOW I HAD A CHOICE WITH MINE, BUT WE ARE TALKING ABOUT RHODRI] \endash  But Jeanne tops my idea by suggesting Sir Cynan is a very good match, both as a known companion for Morgaine, but also good as a joining of Sarum and Silchester.  Once again my love shows her astute wisdom.  I go to speak to Morgaine and as I\rquote m about to knock on her door, I overhear from within her questioning of \ldblquote Did my lord like my playing?\rdblquote   I am shocked to recognize the voice of Unseleighe Prince replying \endash  Pushing open the door, barely seemed to surprise them for they turned to look at me and then they just disappeared.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Quickly, I run to Jeanne, shouting that Aleel\rquote s taken Morgaine.  She lets me rant till I can talk normally, then she finds out what I\rquote m talking about.  She races to Morgaine\rquote s room and stops at the doorway.  Closing her eyes for a while, she then moves into the room and then jumps out the window and changes in a shimmer into the form of the Raven which then flies off. 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Striding down to the hall, I order servants to prepare my horse and gather supplies for a week.  As Sir Gilbert, who is acting as my Seneschal enters, he asks when do we ride.  Truly a good friend, but I instruct him to protect Broadchalke while I\rquote m gone.  I return to Morgaine\rquote s room to await my love\rquote s return with what she has learnt.  But as night falls, the weight of the rest of the world returns and I must take care of my family.  For the next four days of waiting, I find I cling to Arthur and my children …
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Arcavius and Cynan return from their embassy to Dorset, bringing word that the Praetor agrees to this alliance if Earl Robert can provide 10 knights to support him.  But that is almost forgotten as I bring them up to speed on what happened.  We travel to Sarum and pass word of the embassy to Dorset, and also of my current urgent mission.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}}\pard \fi-360\li360\nowidctlpar\tx360{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls1\pnrnot0\pnindent360\pnhang{\pntxtb -}}\ls1\adjustright {Travel to Sauvernake Forest and speak to Puck (he comes when I call!)   Although I am in great disfavour with Oberon, I tell Puck to pass a message to Oberon of what has happened to Morgaine.  He wants to know what I\rquote m going to do, and I reply I\rquote m going to talk to Aleel & his quick reply is \ldblquote I suggest not like last time.\rdblquote   He offers to pass the word on to Oberon if I promise to reward him as my honour suggests.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}We go to Avesbury circle \endash  Puck is very unhappy & the horses are spooked \endash  blood sacrifice \endash  Red Cap comes (like the anti-Puck) \endash  we butt heads verbally \endash  I make the point that I ask politely here where I could have visited Aleel\rquote s circle as before \endash  Red Cap goes into the stone \endash  after a while he comes back & says Aleel welcomes the foster-father of his new companion \endash  then the Red  Cap bows us through the stone \endash  Arcavius tries first & his faith bounces him back thrice - & then Cynan, me  & Hwyll
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Tunnel like a postern gate into a cavern \endash  carved statues of mortal realm which eventually pass to non-mundane statues \endash  (I get the feeling they are not carved statues) \endash  after five times of passing a flying raven statue (…) , I call the Red Cap to take us to Aleel, but he says he wanted me to recognise the artwork and how good it was \endash  I do a doubletake on the Raven statue and its }{\b\ul Jeanne }{(crit. Recognise \endash  into shock-cum-rage)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}The Red Cap takes us past a guard named Otho the Troll (looking into his eyes is a confusing experience \endash  the absence of any intelligence gives me vertigo) \endash  we approach the sounds of a party \endash  the Red-Cap taunts me with words that the wedding has started \endash  when he asks for our invitations, we gate-crash \endash  what we see is ten-times wilder than Beltaine behaviour
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Aleel is on a raised dais, with a female in raven gear & mask \endash  there is also a capering big-eared fool, which is strangely monkey-like \endash  The Red-Cap makes a parody of a bow & announces me but forgets my name \endash  I announce myself \endash  Aleel welcomes me & we talk \endash  I ask for the Red-Cap to bring my wife in & Aleel acts innocently (? hah!)
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Then the bird-lady rises & puts her arm in Aleels & whispers to him.  Aleel smiles <SHUDDER> & says he is not the one I should be asking; but at the same time, he also looked surprised and a little concerned.  Then it is my turn to be surprised … it was Morgaine who petrified my love.  She says that Jeanne tried to take her away \endash  away from being a queen, from getting something she deserved & she wasn\rquote t being handed everything [?] \endash  she had also been saying that Jeanne was jealous of her.  I say I came to the wedding.  Smiling mischievously, she asks if I will drink to her at her wedding.  I can only respond with agreement if I can share it with my wife (this I would do for her, no one else), while my more sensible companions vigorously refuse.  She once again asks will I not even drink to her, again I can only refuse.  She finally asks won\rquote t I even dance with her.  Her eyes are bright with unshed tears, but she still smiles her smile.  \ldblquote For what I felt for you, I acquiesce.\rdblquote 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}We begin the dance and then the music joined us.  The rest of the court joined in the dancing, but it was shortly thereafter that the music changed.  We were caught in the music, which skirled around and around more and more frenetically.  Hwyll had joined in the dancing, but Cynan managed to resist the lure.  Cynan knew we were caught and had to hit me on the back of my head twice to bring me out of it.  It had drawn me from the dance by appealing to one of my most basic instincts (fighting).  As we are bundled out (carefully as I had drawn my sword because I had been under attack), I am surprised to find we have been joined by a couple costumed as a wolf and a bear.  It is our enigmatic, occasional companions, Leda and Tyler. She is holding a 4\rquote  dude (garbed as a misshapen sparrow).
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Leda says we must leave }{\ul now}{.  We go to Jeanne\rquote s statue.  With my sword still drawn and after Leda\rquote s calm, yet measuredly terrifying, polite inquiries of the Unseleighe \ldblquote Sparrow\rdblquote , the \ldblquote Sparrow\rdblquote  thinks it is best to transform Jeanne back to her natural state.  Unfortunately, in his eagerness to do so as quickly as possible, he failed on his first few tries.  The Raven statue transmutes from stone to flesh and she collapses to the ground.  Dropping my sword, I too fall .. to my knees and cradle her.  \ldblquote Oh, Jeanne!\rdblquote 
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}But there is no time to tarry, for a loud scream comes from the far side of the gardens as something huge and dark and Fae this way cometh.  Uncertain of whether we could reach the exit we had entered this realm through, Arcavius says he knows of a way to go to another realm.  He gets us all to hold hands, and suddenly we find ourselves outside of the Lady\rquote s castle.  When we enter and are directed to the Lady, the Lady and Leda do the silent stare (which can mean anything, but always means trouble).  I beg of the Lady to please help my love \endash  she does \endash  I answer all her question truthfully and without hesitation, distractedly even \endash  answering about why Morgaine did what she did depresses me in true knightly style, and I am at an all-time low where someone could have put a knife in my hand and it would have done the rest by instinct.  But then Jeanne caws, and once again my knees are punished as I throw myself to her side on a stool by the fire.  She shimmers once again and returns to me as I know her best. Huge, humongous hug.  As we are embraced for a while, I answer a few more questions until food and drinks arrive.  As everyone begins to eat, I begin (and finish just as fast) to pass out --- By the way, I don\rquote t recall anything after the start of the dance.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Late the next morning, I\rquote m given something }{\ul really}{ foul-smelling and foul-tasting (it must be }{\ul really}{ good for me) & I feel a lot better \endash  I share a walk with Jeanne and I console her after she has had her first setback \endash  she wants to go home, directly \endash  go looking for my fellow knights and ask them what happened in the time that I can\rquote t remember (I\rquote m surprised again about the arrivals of Leda and Tyler and again by their mysterious absence now) \endash  I tell them we\rquote re going home \endash  I then go to find my gracious hostess. After introductions are made between the Lady and my wife, and a strangely nice and quiet chat, she kindly sends Hwyll, Jeanne and I back home the day after we arrived at Avesbury
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Our fellow two knights are returned at the same time to Avesbury with their squires
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\fs20 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 -\tab}Time passes \endash  Jeanne improves, but she always has the loss of her invincibility and the fact that Morgaine (her successor, her adopted daughter) had betrayed her \endash  word is passed to Sarum of the situation and our prior mission to take the messages of the proposed alliance to the other big lords is passed to other respected messengers.
\par }\pard \nowidctlpar\tx360\adjustright {
\par 501 \endash  my sister, Astrigis, has gone missing.  She had married a Cymric merchant of Hereford in Gloucester.  She was lost in the Dean\rquote s Forest, the which surrounds Hereford all the way into the Cambrian mountains.
\par }}